{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he went up to the shearers of his sheep.</b> He would go up there regularly to find comfort, so that he would set his mind on the flock and forget his bereavement. And it was told to Tamar that he goes up there every day regularly, and she lay in wait for him on one of those days. Or perhaps Judah was a great man in the land and people would gather there to make a feast at shearing time, like a king's banquet, and the poor would go there, and it was told to her before his going up."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:41:34.217228431Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}